// Title: Scripted Diagnostics Turn Off Check Enabled - Registry
// Sigma ID: 7d995e63-ec83-4aa3-89d5-8a17b5c87c86
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Christopher Peacock @securepeacock, SCYTHE @scythe_io
// Date: 2022-06-15 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects enabling TurnOffCheck which can be used to bypass defense of MSDT Follina vulnerability
// False positives:
//   - Administrator actions
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20220629042017/https://twitter.com/wdormann/status/1537075968568877057
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_enabling_turnoffcheck.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\ScriptedDiagnostics\\TurnOffCheck" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)"
